    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7b2ff043",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: how_to_pick_chicks_in_auschwitz; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person using a shovel and broom in what appears to be a grim, industrial setting, juxtaposed with the text 'how to pick chicks in auschwitz.' This is a hateful and deeply offensive meme that equates the act of selecting people (implied to be victims) in a concentration camp with a trivial or sexualized activity ('pick chicks'). The reference to Auschwitz, a site of genocide and mass murder, is used in a grotesque and dehumanizing manner to trivialize the Holocaust and its victims. The meme's intent is to shock, provoke, and demean, leveraging the horror of historical atrocity to mock or belittle a target group (likely Jewish people or other victims of the Holocaust) by reducing their suffering to a crude, sexualized metaphor. This is a direct attack on the memory of genocide and the dignity of its victims, making it a hateful and harmful piece of content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e86cfb96"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
